<title>UK: VAN OMMEREN TO BUY UK, S.AFRICA TERMINALS.</title>
<headline>VAN OMMEREN TO BUY UK, S.AFRICA TERMINALS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Powell Duffryn Plc said it had entered into conditional agreements to sell its UK and South African terminals businesses to Koninklijke Van Ommeren of Rotterdam for 16.5 million stg in cash.</p>
<p>In a statement, the company added that it was writing down the book value of its three terminals in the U.S. by 15 million stg &quot;to what is now indicated to be their realisable value.&quot;  </p>
<p>In a separate statement, Van Ommeren said it was still in talks about buying Powell Duffryn's chemicals terminals in Bayonne, U.S.</p>
<p>The investment in the South African and British tank storage firms will positively affect Van Ommeren's 1996 net profit, the Dutch company said.</p>
<p>It added that its 49 percent owned unit Compania Mexicana de Terminales was presently building a chemicals storage terminal in the Mexican port of Altamira.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
